// Typecheck-only config that INCLUDES src/**/__tests__.
//
// Why this file exists: tsconfig.json excludes "src/**/__tests__", and vitest
// transpiles without typechecking. Between the two, no test file in this repo
// was ever typechecked — 32 real type errors had accumulated invisibly
// (openclaw-provenance-v3q). `npm run typecheck:tests` closes that hole.
//
// Why the module settings differ from tsconfig.json: the build emits CommonJS
// (module: Node16 + no "type": "module" in package.json), but vitest executes
// test files as ESM. Modeling the build's CJS semantics here would reject
// `import.meta.url`, which is legal and correct in the environment the tests
// actually run in. So this config describes vitest's module semantics, while
// tsconfig.json remains the authority on what the shipped build must satisfy.
// Both gates run; neither replaces the other.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler"
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": []
}
